      "content": "Wait, solar acoustic modes? I haven't seen much about that in standard textbooks. If these are causing felt vibrations at ground level, does the resonance usually happen in specific geographic regions or at certain times of day? I've noticed the hum seems to peak when the sky looks a certain way. Could the local topography or something in the atmosphere be magnifying these effects in my specific area?",
